  "style": {
    "id": "wind-walker",
    "name": "Wind Walker",
    "description": "A kinetic walking sculpture on a bright low-tide beach: a skeletal creature of pale plastic tubing, black cable ties and cloth sails whose twelve legs are identical planar bar linkages (a straight-line four-bar feeding a pantograph, solved in closed form by circle–circle intersections) hung on one shared crankshaft, each station a sixth of a turn later, so rigid sticks step in a travelling wave. Body travel and height are locked to the lowest foot, so planted feet do not slide; footprints and step thuds come from the same plan. Opens on ONE leg as a diagram in sea mist (ink centre-lines, crank circle, the foot's flat-bottomed loop traced as a glowing path), then the mist lifts to reveal the whole creature striding across the sand.",
